# provider-usage: Claude's reader takes a warning's line whole (a warning has fields after its windows),
# and the newest reading across the logs, not the newest file's, stopping at a file older than the one in hand.
# events.c.log's line is stamped after its file's own time, which can't happen in a real log, on purpose: a
# truthful older line gives the same answer whether the scan stops or not, so only this one shows that it stopped.
