# provider-usage's Claude API credits: only the API instance's spend counts (never the subscription's),
# the soonest-expiring grant is drawn first and the next takes what it can't cover (also across an
# expiry), an expired grant has nothing left and spend after its expiry never touches it, only spend after
# the one Console reading counts (and grants read at different times are an error), a result logged twice counts once, a line with no per-model costs counts the rise of its
# session's total, malformed lines are skipped, a log untouched since the balance is not read, spend is
# never taken below zero, no credits file leaves the provider out, and a malformed file is an error, not a crash.
